  <static seed="1886" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/FractionSubtractionWordProblems50.pg">
    <statement><p>Brandon and Michele are sharing a pizza. Brandon ate <m>{{\frac{2}{9}}}</m> of the pizza, and Michele ate <m>{{\frac{1}{5}}}</m> of the pizza. How much more pizza did Brandon eat than Michele?</p>
<p>Brandon ate <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> more of the pizza than Michele ate.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{1}{45}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To find the difference of two numbers, we use subtraction:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{2}{9}}} - {{\frac{1}{5}}} 
      \amp = \frac{2 \cdot 5}{9 \cdot 5}-\frac{1 \cdot 9}{5 \cdot 9} \\
      \amp = \frac{10}{45} - \frac{9}{45} \\
      \amp = \frac{10-9}{45} \\
      
      \amp = {{\frac{1}{45}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Brandon ate <m>{{\frac{1}{45}}}</m> more of the pizza than Michele ate.</p>
</solution>
